          "meaning_hint": "Imagine you’re the sun, working all day. Of course you get tired. This is a good excuse to go to bed at night and get some rest. Feel how sore and hot and sweaty and exhausted you are after a hard day’s work of being the sun.",
          "meaning_mnemonic": "The <span style="background-color: #00aaff; color: white; padding: 0 4px; border-radius: 3px;">sun</span> has an <span style="background-color: #00aaff; color: white; padding: 0 4px; border-radius: 3px;">excuse</span> for disappearing at <span style="background-color: #ff00aa; color: white; padding: 0 4px; border-radius: 3px;">night</span>. The sun gets really tired, same as anyone else – so when night rolls around the sun excuses itself and goes to sleep. It’s a valid excuse.",
